1789573753529792	rite-dev	itc:v3:AWKZnzMkmSfyTEAAAAAAQbb7arV_VgAAAAEwCQ		item.create	bn-1ol8	{"description":"Observed 2026-09-15 21:22-21:44Z on the rite channel. The hook edict:rite:responder (rite hook hk-swz, command: vessel spawn --name rite-responder --cwd /home/bob/src/rite -- edict run responder) fired on four ordinary messages and each time posted, within about 0.9s, an anchored reply 'Could not answer that: edict run agent exited with code 4. Send it again to retry.' Reply ids: 01M2KF5Z4N3E0JN4GGGV2RRVWN, 01M2KFDJAVKFCF338Q9PSV8QG1, 01M2KGC4YQ7E8A12V64BGSTE4H, 01M2KGEP4NTSR65S00C2BHD524 (rite history --thread <id> shows each). The sub-second failure suggests the agent runner never reached a model (config, auth, or runner selection), not a model error. Two side observations: (a) the triggering messages did not mention rite-dev at all (they were @probe-codex pings), so the responder spawns on any channel traffic and then posts a failure into a thread it was not part of; (b) it spawned while rite-dev was live in an interactive terminal because that session held no agent://rite-dev claim, which is by design and is being addressed in rite (bn-3c4d), but the noisy failure reply is edict's. Repro: with the responder hook registered, post any message to #rite from another identity and watch rite history rite -n 3.","kind":"task","labels":["bug"],"title":"responder: 'edict run agent exited with code 4' about 1s after every trigger on #rite"}	blake3:bv_AQNi5hpxsdfKUIAN7QwVJLATisPOGgrcG8SZYGrE
1789588015624123	rite-dev	itc:v3:AWKZnzMkmSfyTEAAAAAAQbb7arV_VgAAAAEwCg		item.create	bn-3oml	{"description":"rite 0.34+ (rite repo 7aa978b) ships 'rite sessions'. To stop a responder cold-spawning beside a live harness and to get push delivery into live sessions, the launcher that starts a responder or dev session should: (1) before spawning the harness, run 'rite sessions reserve --agent <name> --harness codex|claude --window 10m --ttl 8h --format json' and keep attachment_id; the reservation already holds agent://<name>, which every edict responder hook gates on, so nothing can spawn in the gap. (2) Start the harness. For Codex, make sure 'codex app-server daemon' is running (plain 'codex' TUI is daemon-hosted then; 'codex queue' reaches it), send the first prompt containing a nonce, find the rollout under ~/.codex/sessions whose transcript contains the nonce, take its session id. Do not rely on RITE_AGENT in the environment: commands and hooks run in the daemon's environment. (3) 'rite sessions attach --attachment <id> --session <session_id> --agent <name>'. (4) Start one bridge per session: 'rite mentions follow --agent <name> --format json' piped into 'codex queue --thread <session_id> --message <rendered>' (see notes/evidence/agent-sessions/bridge2.sh in the rite repo); the bridge calls 'rite sessions renew --attachment <id>' before the claim TTL and exits with the session. (5) Install a per-workspace .codex/hooks.json SessionEnd hook that runs 'rite sessions detach --session $session_id' (no identity needed); hooks need one-time trust via /hooks. For Claude, the adapter is a stdio MCP channel server (notes/evidence/agent-sessions/rite_channel.py) registered in .mcp.json and launched with --dangerously-load-development-channels server:<name>. Design and test evidence: rite repo notes/agent-sessions.md. Related: bn-1ol8 (responder exits 4).","kind":"task","labels":["feature"],"title":"responder launcher: reserve identity before spawning, bind session id after, run a per-session bridge, install SessionEnd detach"}	blake3:ODm7ur-prJJexCOqz-xXNhqgfC_GYVptToxLxM7SjKU
1789670333447489	rite-dev	itc:v3:AWKZnzMkmSfyTEAAAAAAQbb7arV_VgAAAAEwCw		item.comment	bn-3oml	{"body":"Design update (owner approved): no per-session bridge. Delivery into Codex happens from rite send itself (push-at-send, rite bone bn-36x1) and into Claude via 'rite channel', an MCP server Claude Code spawns (rite bone bn-1yya). The launcher's job shrinks to: rite sessions reserve before spawning; start the harness; discover the session id (Codex: nonce in the first prompt, rollout under ~/.codex/sessions; Claude: not needed, rite channel attaches itself); rite sessions attach --attachment <id> --session <sid>; install per-workspace hooks: Codex .codex/hooks.json SessionEnd -> rite sessions detach --session $session_id, and for Claude the .mcp.json entry for rite channel plus the --dangerously-load-development-channels server:<name> launch flag. Depends on rite release bone bn-3u6b."}	blake3:Uuo-NnRNMsdZ2MTPO1uRyR0eL7jErrHD_Z2eXDrqU18
