1790185544963247	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAQ		item.create	bn-2f92	{"description":"# Problem\nThe generated workflow docs never tell anyone to commit Seal review state. Seal keeps each review as an event log under .seal/reviews/<id>/ in the workspace where it was created. .seal/.gitignore ignores only index.db, so the logs are meant to be tracked. But no step in finish, worker-loop, review-response or merge-check commits them. After `maw ws merge --destroy` the reviews are gone from trunk, and `seal reviews list` at the repo root shows \"No reviews yet\".\n\nObserved in ~/src/continuum on 2026-09-23. A lead agent ran 13 dedicated security reviews over one session. None reached trunk until they were restored by hand (continuum commit 8b16fb4). A second cause: `maw ws sync` refuses a workspace with untracked files, and untracked .seal/reviews is one. So the agent moved it aside to sync, and it was then destroyed with the workspace.\n\n# Expected flow (user's stated expectation)\nCreate a maw workspace, do the work, run the review, commit the changes AND the review in the workspace, then merge and destroy. Review logs are tracked with the repo.\n\n# Defects to fix\n1. Missing step. After the LGTM (and after any lead-owned record edits), commit .seal/reviews/<id>/ in the workspace, for example `maw exec $WS -- git add .seal/reviews/<id> && git commit -m \"chore: seal review <id>\"`. A committed review also keeps `maw ws sync` from refusing on untracked files.\n2. Contradiction. review-response.md says \"Commit nothing after the LGTM\", and `seal reviews mark-merged` exits 1 when the approval does not cover the current code. But the LGTM vote itself writes .seal/reviews/<id>/events.jsonl, so committing the review is always a commit after the approval. Either seal exempts commits that touch only .seal/ from the staleness check (needs a seal change; file it there), or the docs direct `--allow-stale-approval` with a reason for a .seal-only commit. The first is cleaner.\n3. Ordering bug in merge-check.md. Step 1 merges with --destroy, then step 2 runs `maw exec $WS -- seal reviews mark-merged <id>` inside the workspace that was just destroyed. worker-loop.md instead marks merged before the merge, which leaves that event uncommitted in a workspace about to be destroyed. Pick one: mark-merged on trunk after the merge (`seal reviews mark-merged <id> --commit <merge sha>`), then commit that event on trunk, or record it in the workspace before merging, if seal can know the final commit.\n\n# Where to change\n- src/templates/docs/worker-loop.md, review-response.md, merge-check.md, finish.md (and review-request.md or security-review.md if they describe the post-LGTM steps)\n- src/templates/agents-managed.md.jinja (the Reviews section: \"Do not commit after the LGTM\")\n- src/commands/protocol/finish.rs and src/commands/protocol/merge.rs, and the emitted step lists in src/commands/worker_loop.rs and src/commands/dev_loop/prompt.rs\n- eval scripts that assert the old order (evals/scripts/e10-*, e11-*, e12-*)\n\n# Acceptance\n- Following the generated docs step by step leaves every review log committed on trunk, and `seal reviews list` at the repo root shows it with status merged.\n- No step runs a command inside a destroyed workspace.\n- `edict protocol merge` and `edict protocol finish` output matches the docs.\n- The docs no longer contradict each other on committing after the LGTM.","kind":"bug","title":"Workflow docs never commit Seal review logs; post-LGTM commit rule contradicts it; merge-check runs mark-merged in a destroyed workspace"}	blake3:7TvwvziATCzsW5umqhZu-Jgc_XGY0_L8PZCpDYtIv6g
