1790470540335515	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-1ol8	{"field":"title","value":"Responder: sub-second 'edict run agent exited with code 4' replies on every #rite trigger"}	blake3:-sAoSrAvjssmJ3yZUgSWBdZqRXUyvmwc9B_Rj9fDfOI
1790470540341414	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-1ol8	{"field":"description","value":"Observed 2026-09-15 21:22-21:44Z on #rite. Hook edict:rite:responder (hk-swz: vessel spawn --name rite-responder --cwd /home/bob/src/rite -- edict run responder) fired on four ordinary messages and each time posted within ~0.9s: 'Could not answer that: edict run agent exited with code 4. Send it again to retry.' Reply ids: 01M2KF5Z4N3E0JN4GGGV2RRVWN, 01M2KFDJAVKFCF338Q9PSV8QG1, 01M2KGC4YQ7E8A12V64BGSTE4H, 01M2KGEP4NTSR65S00C2BHD524.\n\nCode facts (groomed 2026-09-26): exit 4 is ExitError::ToolFailed (src/error.rs:43) from the inner 'edict run agent' (src/commands/run_agent.rs ~378-425). The outer callers (src/commands/dev_loop/mod.rs:997, src/commands/worker_loop.rs:818) bail with only the exit code, so the real reason is dropped before report_turn_failure (src/commands/responder.rs:778) posts it.\n\nSide observations: (a) the triggers were @probe-codex pings, not addressed to rite-dev, yet the responder posted a failure into their thread; (b) it spawned while rite-dev was live interactively because no agent://rite-dev claim was held — addressed in rite (bn-3c4d), out of scope here.\n\nExit gate (manual): all children done, and posting a non-addressed message to #rite from another identity produces either a real answer or no reply at all — never a bare 'exited with code N'. Verified by a human on the live channel."}	blake3:PxknOlG3YLgLhU0bX98_ByoU1n32fPXMxdpKX0qTa0I
1790470540344135	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-1ol8	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:920JVqAVqtxUpvvkQiXnVsr_rvtXeRQmUAs1gzOCY-8
1790470540365018	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-1ol8	{"field":"labels","value":{"action":"add","label":"goal:manual"}}	blake3:GYNVAYVvFR7cViHhRDX_coCYIsa38rbyQWcHDZpfsr8
1790470540384716	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-1ol8	{"field":"labels","value":{"action":"remove","label":"bug"}}	blake3:0aeP3Pat-kbW6L5o7zWNOK0OpcwU70544OoklHM0e3A
1790470541608390	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2kgk	{"description":"dev_loop/mod.rs:997 and worker_loop.rs:818 bail 'edict run agent exited with code {code}' and discard the child's stderr, which holds the ToolFailed/Config message. Capture the child's stderr (bounded tail, e.g. last 20 lines) and include the first meaningful error line in the anyhow error, so report_turn_failure posts e.g. 'Could not answer that: claude: not authenticated (exit 4)'.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Both call sites share one helper; no duplicated capture logic.\n- tests/run_agent_integration.rs (or a unit test with a fake runner script) asserts the propagated message contains the inner error text.\n- Secrets hygiene: stderr tail is truncated to 200 chars in the channel reply (already done in report_turn_failure) and never includes env dumps.","kind":"bug","parent":"bn-1ol8","size":"s","title":"Propagate inner 'edict run agent' failure reason to callers and responder replies"}	blake3:ZihW6lulCW2JUMcliBSFusqm23DLBHCNNFvfq1UmQgk
1790470541745394	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2d57	{"description":"With the reason now visible (depends on the propagation fix), reproduce: register the responder hook for a sandbox project (RITE_DATA_DIR=<tmp>, see bn-3cud), post any message from another identity, read the failure reply. Likely candidates: runner/model selection in the rite project's .edict.toml, missing auth for the selected runner, or an invalid model pool entry.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Root cause recorded as a comment here.\n- Fix lands in edict (config validation, default, or clearer error) or, if the cause is project config, 'edict doctor'/sync flags it.\n- Regression test covering the specific failure path.","kind":"bug","parent":"bn-1ol8","size":"s","title":"Diagnose and fix the sub-second exit-4 responder failure in the rite project"}	blake3:RkRJ4b_W43VwDuoW-jqyj1HIFYHmyltHBK61YOiZdqE
1790470541874203	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-qfr6	{"description":"The responder spawns on any channel traffic, then posts 'Could not answer that…' into threads addressed to other agents (@probe-codex pings on #rite). Decide and implement: when the triggering message is not addressed to this responder's identity (no @mention, not a reply to it, not a DM), a turn failure is logged and counted (edict.responder.turn_failures_total) but not posted to the channel.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Unit tests for the addressed/not-addressed decision (mention, reply-to-own-message, DM, plain traffic).\n- Integration test: failure on a non-addressed message produces no rite send.\n- Update the responder section of AGENTS.md and the managed template if behavior is described there.","kind":"bug","parent":"bn-1ol8","size":"s","title":"Responder must not post turn-failure replies into threads it was not addressed in"}	blake3:CwF3rcvay4RKY220UzskpgrFJu_Xi8ATE_0TQyND26g
1790470566593313	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-2d57	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-2kgk"}	blake3:0R8DUMnreEFEg-PVInoOO5GLZHDghvqSAJYUSUGx8M8
1790470566636275	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-3cud	{"field":"title","value":"edict init/sync must never touch a rite data dir the caller did not name"}	blake3:DjOj9ClCCo0vOX3Fvp6Co2fwnEgI7QUE-smAytq5_tE
1790470566641745	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-3cud	{"field":"description","value":"Running `edict init` against a throwaway directory registered a router hook in the real rite data dir (~/.local/share/rite), taking the live hook set from 42 to 43. Found and removed manually (hk-k20, channel tmp-lswaiazzwu, cwd /tmp/tmp.LSWaiaZzwu).\n\nReproduced on 2026-08-09 while rendering the managed AGENTS.md template to verify a change. The only way to see what the template produces is to run edict against a real project, and doing that mutates live state.\n\nWhy it matters: those hooks are not inert. Each fires `vessel spawn` to launch a real AI agent in a real repo. A hook registered for a temp directory points at a cwd that will not exist later. On this machine there are 42 live hooks across ~25 projects, so contaminating that set is not a cosmetic problem.\n\nThere is also a second-order effect. Any contributor or agent testing an edict template change has the same choice: skip verification, or contaminate live state. That pushes people toward not verifying, which is how the `rite wait --mention` error survived across 15 repos.\n\nWanted:\n- A `--dry-run` on `sync` (and `init`) that renders and reports without writing anything outside the target directory.\n- Or honor `RITE_DATA_DIR` consistently so a caller can point hook registration at a sandbox, and document that as the supported way to test.\n- Either way, `edict init`/`sync` should never write to a rite data dir the caller did not name, and should say what it is about to register before doing it.\n\nNote `rite hooks` has no in-place modify, so a wrongly-registered hook can only be removed and re-added, not corrected. Tracked separately in rite.\n\n--- Groomed 2026-09-26 ---\nCode facts: rite already resolves RITE_DATA_DIR (rite src/core/project.rs data_dir()), and edict's rite subprocesses inherit the env, so pointing a sandbox at a tmp dir likely works today but is untested and undocumented. There is no --dry-run on init or sync ('sync --check' reports staleness only).\n\nExit gate (manual): a contributor can verify a template change end to end (init + sync against a throwaway dir) with the documented recipe, and the live ~/.local/share/rite hook count is unchanged afterward. Verified by a human."}	blake3:HdDAN2RnMlSwAK87uYsYJoYy3SvxnmK-crLAnMryGkk
1790470566644900	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-3cud	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:xUyCf8uxv1uwLS8ts7oliRwQqHYFTJ68ZLM0j5nf3jI
1790470566668076	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-3cud	{"field":"labels","value":{"action":"add","label":"goal:manual"}}	blake3:5OOg_P-1TSI2AyjTfD7houc2Eq_9UjQSDDZjSBFDyaw
