1790471755123583	edict-12wg8u	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2adz	{"description":"Follow-up from bn-qfr6. The router hook wakes the responder on every channel message, so @probe-codex pings on #rite each started a full triage agent run. src/commands/responder_addressing.rs classify() already knows when a message is NotAddressed. Add a cheap pre-check in Responder::run() that exits quietly (no agent run, no post) when the trigger batch is NotAddressed, keeping Unknown/Addressed behavior unchanged. Consider whether a rite hook --mention/filter is the better fix instead. Tests: pre-check skips on other-agent-only mentions, runs on plain traffic, commands, DMs, and on Unknown. Update AGENTS.md responder section.","kind":"task","size":"s","title":"Responder: skip the agent run for messages that only @mention other agents"}	blake3:Ios-E0wyah958LU8dLU0SOMQq6ZoeVnb9baHK8DI9Nk
